# Check that the Kitsune options are visible in opt under the appropriate
# category. This is not intended to be a comprehensive check of all options. It
# merely exists to ensure that the categories of Kitsune options are not lost.
#
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The "developer" options are not visible when simply asking for help
#
# RUN: opt -help 2>&1 | FileCheck %s -check-prefix HELP
#
# HELP-NOT: Kitsune Developer Options
# HELP: Kitsune Options
# HELP: --kitrt-verbose
# HELP: --tapir
# HELP: --tapir-cuda-arch=
# HELP: --tapir-hip-arch=
# HELP: --tapir-verbose
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The "developer" options are visible when hidden options are included. The
# developer options are intended to override the default behavior of Kitsune's
# passes and are typically, but not always, prefixed with some short form
# indicating the pass.
#
# RUN: opt -help-hidden 2>&1 | FileCheck %s -check-prefix HIDDEN
#
# HIDDEN: Kitsune Developer Options
# HIDDEN: cgfb-###
# HIDDEN: cgfb-ptxas-O1
# HIDDEN: emb-O0
# HIDDEN: emb-inline-all
# HIDDEN: emb-print-pipeline-passes
# HIDDEN: Kitsune Options
# HIDDEN: --kitrt-verbose
# HIDDEN: --tapir
